{
 "method": "forecast_v2 (pre-registered backtest winner). grain = latest pre-January NASS grain-area forecast (Nov 14 2025; Sep 12 2025 where November omits the state) as is (NASS: latest pre-January NASS grain forecast as is). silage = BLEND_PD: (S1 + S2) / 2, i.e. the average of method D (forecast/estimate_2025.py, shares over 2022-2024) and last year's silage acres. Chosen by the lowest acre-weighted absolute % error over 2018-2024 state-years among 6 pre-registered candidates. SE = estimate x the backtest RMS relative error of its size class; 95% range = estimate +/- z SE with z the 95th percentile of backtest |error|/SE; covered_by_95_interval is leave-one-year-out. US: SE = estimate x RMS of the backtest US relative errors, 95% range = +/- t(0.975, n-1) SE. Each convergence date is re-estimated with only what was known then and gets its own range, calibrated on the backtest errors of that release.",
